WEBVTT

gender-03-1
00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.560
Pregnancy takes about forty weeks.

gender-03-2
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.320
Raising a child takes at least eighteen
years.

gender-03-3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.480
Those forty weeks involve her body. Who
assigned her the eighteen years?

gender-03-4
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:11.840
Let's unpack the word “motherhood.”

gender-03-5
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.680
Pregnancy, childbirth and breastfeeding
do involve a particular body.

gender-03-6
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.620
Their pain and risks are real. They
should not be dismissed.

gender-03-7
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:20.820
But what comes next?

gender-03-8
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.060
Soothing a baby at night, changing
diapers, tracking vaccines, attending

gender-03-9
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:24.700
school meetings.

gender-03-10
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.076
The child has a fever: take leave. The
child starts school: quit work. Which of

gender-03-11
00:00:30.076 --> 00:00:30.400
these

gender-03-12
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.020
requires a uterus?

gender-03-13
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.360
Not one.

gender-03-14
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.620
Yet they are bundled into one word:

gender-03-15
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.080
motherhood. What ties the bundle together
is not biology, but a sentence:

gender-03-16
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.180
“You're the mother.”

gender-03-17
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:45.882
Some say women are naturally better at
childcare. The evidence? Usually, that

gender-03-18
00:00:45.882 --> 00:00:47.240
women have always done it.

gender-03-19
00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.500
That uses the outcome to prove the cause.

gender-03-20
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.813
A 2014 Israeli study found that fathers
who were primary caregivers showed

gender-03-21
00:00:53.813 --> 00:00:57.718
activity in brain regions linked to
emotional vigilance close to that of

gender-03-22
00:00:57.718 --> 00:01:01.623
primary-caregiving mothers. The more
hands-on care fathers provided, the

gender-03-23
00:01:01.623 --> 00:01:04.660
stronger the connections between relevant
brain regions.

gender-03-24
00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:09.027
One study cannot settle this. But it
raises a question: how much of what we

gender-03-25
00:01:09.027 --> 00:01:09.780
call “instinct”

gender-03-26
00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.340
is skill acquired by those who started
first?

gender-03-27
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.860
At this point, we must mention someone.

gender-03-28
00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.440
In 1970, in The Dialectic of Sex,
Shulamith Firestone went further than

gender-03-29
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.360
anyone else. She did not represent all
radical feminists,

gender-03-30
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:27.308
but she pushed the question to one of its
deepest points. She saw the division of

gender-03-31
00:01:27.308 --> 00:01:29.980
reproductive labor itself as the root of
women's oppression.

gender-03-32
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.898
She imagined using technology, including
artificial wombs, to free women from

gender-03-33
00:01:33.898 --> 00:01:37.260
childbearing, then making both
reproduction and childrearing society's

gender-03-34
00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:37.980
responsibility.

gender-03-35
00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.782
That is radical. But in one respect, not
radical enough. She placed the root in

gender-03-36
00:01:42.782 --> 00:01:43.420
the uterus.

gender-03-37
00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.071
But if the problem is the uterus, why are
mothers also assigned those eighteen

gender-03-38
00:01:48.071 --> 00:01:51.922
years that require no uterus? What
oppresses women is not “she can give

gender-03-39
00:01:51.922 --> 00:01:54.580
birth.” It is society then signing on her
behalf:

gender-03-40
00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.680
“Since you can give birth, everything
else

gender-03-41
00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.320
comes bundled with it, and is yours too.”

gender-03-42
00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.243
Even if artificial wombs became
widespread tomorrow, as long as “you're

gender-03-43
00:02:02.243 --> 00:02:03.280
the mother” remains,

gender-03-44
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:07.580
the same person would likely still get up
at night, take leave and quit work.

gender-03-45
00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:12.120
Technology may remove those forty weeks,
but not those eighteen years.

gender-03-46
00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:15.495
And sharing those eighteen years does not
require waiting for technology. We can

gender-03-47
00:02:15.495 --> 00:02:15.980
start today.

gender-03-48
00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.260
So the truly radical question is not how
to escape childbearing. It is:

gender-03-49
00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.420
Why should giving birth become an IOU?

gender-03-50
00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:30.652
It reads: you gave birth, so you owe.
Your time, your career, a lifetime of

gender-03-51
00:02:30.652 --> 00:02:31.920
being on call.

gender-03-52
00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.949
She did not sign it. The signatories are
marriage's default division of labor,

gender-03-53
00:02:35.949 --> 00:02:39.794
“good mother” standards that judge only
mothers, and workplaces assuming someone

gender-03-54
00:02:39.794 --> 00:02:41.620
at home will always pick up the slack.

gender-03-55
00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.100
This does not mean wanting to be a mother
is wrong.

gender-03-56
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.980
The poet Adrienne Rich distinguished two
kinds of motherhood:

gender-03-57
00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:51.440
one is the possible relationship between
women and children;

gender-03-58
00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:57.729
the other is an institution that keeps
that possibility, and all women, under

gender-03-59
00:02:57.729 --> 00:02:58.760
male control.

gender-03-60
00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.440
We want to dismantle the second.

gender-03-61
00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.780
The desire to have children deserves
respect. A life mortgaged to that desire

gender-03-62
00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.200
still deserves to be questioned.

gender-03-63
00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:11.920
So next time you hear “a mother should,”
first ask:

gender-03-64
00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.640
Does this task require a uterus?

gender-03-65
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.340
And if it does not,

gender-03-66
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.700
why should it be the mother's duty?

gender-03-67
00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:21.626
The uterus accounts for forty weeks.
Whoever assigned the remaining eighteen

gender-03-68
00:03:21.626 --> 00:03:23.560
years should answer for that arrangement.

gender-03-69
00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.180
Next time, we ask:

gender-03-70
00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:27.960
when someone says, “I chose this freely,”

gender-03-71
00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.440
should the discussion end?

gender-03-72
00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.040
This is UjiBricks. See you next time.
